  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "A positive integer N≥1N\\ge 1N≥1 is given.\nAn NNN-uple (x1,x2,…,xN)(x_1, x_2, \\dots, x_N)(x1​,x2​,…,xN​) of nonnegative integers is special if, after we remove all entries which are zero, its entries are nondecreasing. For example (0,2,0,0,4,0,4,5,0,0)(0, 2, 0, 0, 4, 0, 4, 5, 0, 0)(0,2,0,0,4,0,4,5,0,0) is special, but (3,2,0)(3, 2, 0)(3,2,0) and (0,1,3,0,0,1,0)(0, 1, 3, 0, 0, 1, 0)(0,1,3,0,0,1,0) are not.\n\nOne can show that there is a unique function μ\\muμ defined on the NNN-uples of nonnegative integers such that, for any NNN-uple x=(x1,x2,…,xN)x=(x_1, x_2,\\dots, x_N)x=(x1​,x2​,…,xN​)\n\\sum_{y \\le x} \\mu(y) =\n\\begin{cases}\n    1 &amp;\\text{ifx is special} \\\\\n    0 &amp;\\text{otherwise}\n\\end{cases},\nwhere the sum ranges over all NNN-uples y=(y1,y2,…,yN)y=(y_1, y_2,\\dots, y_N)y=(y1​,y2​,…,yN​) of nonnegative integers such that yi≤xiy_i\\le x_iyi​≤xi​ for all 1≤i≤N1\\le i\\le N1≤i≤N.\n\nYou are given x=(x1,x2,…,xN)x=(x_1,x_2,\\dots, x_N)x=(x1​,x2​,…,xN​), determine whether μ(x)\\mu(x)μ(x) is 000 or not.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line will contain TTT, the number of test cases. Then the test cases follow.\nThe first line of each test case contains one integer NNN, the size of the tuple considered.\nThe second line of each test case contains NNN integers x1,x2,…,xNx_1, x_2, \\dots, x_Nx1​,x2​,…,xN​, the entries of the given NNN-uple.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, print the string yes if μ(x)=0\\mu(x)=0μ(x)=0 and the string no otherwise. You can print each letter in any case (upper or lower).",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤20 0001 \\leq T \\leq 20\\,0001≤T≤20000",
      "1≤N≤100 0001 \\le N \\le 100\\,0001≤N≤100000",
      "0≤xi≤1090\\le x_i\\le 10^90≤xi​≤109",
      "Sum of NNN over all test cases won't exceed 100 000100\\,000100000"
    ],
